('cinema', 4, 'Which Mexican cinematographer won 3 consecutive Oscars?', 'Emmanuel Lubezki', ARRAY['Roger Deakins', 'Robert Richardson', 'Vittorio Storaro'], 'en', true, 'Emmanuel Lubezki won for Gravity (2014), Birdman (2015), and The Revenant (2016).'),
('cinema', 4, 'Which Michael Haneke film won the Palme d''Or in 2012?', 'Amour', ARRAY['The White Ribbon', 'Caché', 'Funny Games'], 'en', true, 'Amour starring Jean-Louis Trintignant also won the Oscar for Best Foreign Language Film.'),
('cinema', 4, 'Which Thai director won the Palme d''Or for Uncle Boonmee?', 'Apichatpong Weerasethakul', ARRAY['Pen-ek Ratanaruang', 'Wisit Sasanatieng', 'Nontawat Numbenchapol'], 'en', true, 'Uncle Boonmee Who Can Recall His Past Lives won the Palme d''Or in 2010.'),
('cinema', 4, 'Which Greek director made The Lobster and The Favourite?', 'Yorgos Lanthimos', ARRAY['Theo Angelopoulos', 'Costa-Gavras', 'Nikos Koundouros'], 'en', true, 'Yorgos Lanthimos is known for his absurdist and unsettling films.'),
('cinema', 4, 'What is the oldest film festival in the world?', 'The Venice Film Festival', ARRAY['Cannes Film Festival', 'Berlin Film Festival', 'Toronto Film Festival'], 'en', true, 'The Venice Film Festival was founded in 1932, 7 years before the Cannes Film Festival.'),
('cinema', 4, 'Which actor won the Best Actor Oscar for There Will Be Blood?', 'Daniel Day-Lewis', ARRAY['Javier Bardem', 'George Clooney', 'Tommy Lee Jones'], 'en', true, 'Daniel Day-Lewis is the only actor to have won 3 Best Actor Oscars.'),
('cinema', 4, 'Which Paul Thomas Anderson film follows the rise of an oil tycoon?', 'There Will Be Blood', ARRAY['Magnolia', 'Boogie Nights', 'The Master'], 'en', true, 'There Will Be Blood (2007) with Daniel Day-Lewis is inspired by Upton Sinclair''s novel Oil!'),
('cinema', 4, 'Which Scandinavian film movement of the 1990s imposed strict filming rules?', 'Dogme 95', ARRAY['French New Wave', 'Free Cinema', 'Neorealism'], 'en', true, 'Dogme 95 was founded by Lars von Trier and Thomas Vinterberg with a manifesto of rules.'),
('cinema', 4, 'Which Wong Kar-wai film is a classic of romantic Hong Kong cinema?', 'In the Mood for Love', ARRAY['Chungking Express', '2046', 'Happy Together'], 'en', true, 'In the Mood for Love (2000) is considered one of the most beautiful romantic films ever made.'),
('cinema', 4, 'Which Taiwanese director made Crouching Tiger, Hidden Dragon?', 'Ang Lee', ARRAY['Zhang Yimou', 'Wong Kar-wai', 'Chen Kaige'], 'en', true, 'Ang Lee directed Crouching Tiger, Hidden Dragon in 2000, winning the Best Foreign Film Oscar.'),
('cinema', 4, 'Which Russian film by Alexander Sokurov was shot in a single 96-minute take?', 'Russian Ark', ARRAY['Moloch', 'The Sun', 'Faust'], 'en', true, 'Russian Ark (2002) is a technical feat filmed in one take at the Hermitage Museum.'),
('cinema', 4, 'Which French director made Blue Is the Warmest Color, Palme d''Or winner in 2013?', 'Abdellatif Kechiche', ARRAY['Jacques Audiard', 'Arnaud Desplechin', 'Céline Sciamma'], 'en', true, 'Blue Is the Warmest Color won the Palme d''Or at Cannes in 2013.'),
('cinema', 4, 'Which Gus Van Sant film about a school shooting won the Palme d''Or?', 'Elephant', ARRAY['Good Will Hunting', 'Milk', 'My Own Private Idaho'], 'en', true, 'Elephant (2003) won both the Palme d''Or and Best Director Prize at Cannes.'),
('cinema', 4, 'Which Nuri Bilge Ceylan film won the Palme d''Or in 2014?', 'Winter Sleep', ARRAY['Once Upon a Time in Anatolia', 'Three Monkeys', 'The Wild Pear Tree'], 'en', true, 'Winter Sleep is a Turkish drama over 3 hours long that captivated the Cannes jury.'),
('cinema', 4, 'Which director is known for extremely long takes in films like Sátántangó?', 'Béla Tarr', ARRAY['Miklós Jancsó', 'Andrei Tarkovsky', 'Theo Angelopoulos'], 'en', true, 'Béla Tarr is a Hungarian director known for contemplative black-and-white films.'),
('cinema', 4, 'Which filmmaker is associated with the cinema of cruelty including Salò?', 'Pier Paolo Pasolini', ARRAY['Federico Fellini', 'Luchino Visconti', 'Bernardo Bertolucci'], 'en', true, 'Pasolini is known for his provocative films, notably Salò, or the 120 Days of Sodom.'),
('cinema', 4, 'Which Charlie Kaufman film is a movie within a movie within a movie?', 'Adaptation', ARRAY['Being John Malkovich', 'Eternal Sunshine', 'Synecdoche, New York'], 'en', true, 'Adaptation (2002) is a meta screenplay about writing a screenplay adapted from a book.'),
('cinema', 4, 'Which Ruben Östlund film won the Palme d''Or in 2022?', 'Triangle of Sadness', ARRAY['The Square', 'Force Majeure', 'Play'], 'en', true, 'Ruben Östlund is the Swedish director who won two consecutive Palmes d''Or.'),
('cinema', 4, 'Which Gaspar Noé film is famous for its controversial 9-minute single-shot scene?', 'Irréversible', ARRAY['Enter the Void', 'I Stand Alone', 'Love'], 'en', true, 'Irréversible (2002) is told in reverse chronology and contains highly controversial scenes.'),
('cinema', 4, 'Which director made the film Amores Perros that launched New Mexican cinema?', 'Alejandro González Iñárritu', ARRAY['Alfonso Cuarón', 'Guillermo del Toro', 'Carlos Reygadas'], 'en', true, 'Amores Perros (2000) was an international success that launched Iñárritu''s career.'),
('cinema', 4, 'Which director made Stalker, a philosophical sci-fi film about a mysterious zone?', 'Andrei Tarkovsky', ARRAY['Sergei Eisenstein', 'Andrei Konchalovsky', 'Alexander Sokurov'], 'en', true, 'Tarkovsky''s Stalker (1979) is a philosophical film about a mysterious zone.'),
('cinema', 4, 'Which Claire Denis film explores colonial themes with Isabelle Huppert?', 'White Material', ARRAY['Beau Travail', 'Trouble Every Day', '35 Shots of Rum'], 'en', true, 'White Material (2009) is set in an African country caught in civil war.'),
('cinema', 4, 'Which hand-coloring process did Georges Méliès use for his films?', 'Stencil coloring', ARRAY['Technicolor', 'Autochrome', 'Tinting'], 'en', true, 'Georges Méliès colored his films frame by frame using stencils.'),
('cinema', 4, 'Which Terrence Malick film features a philosophical voice-over about war and nature?', 'The Thin Red Line', ARRAY['Days of Heaven', 'The Tree of Life', 'Badlands'], 'en', true, 'The Thin Red Line (1998) is set during the Battle of Guadalcanal in World War II.');
INSERT INTO questions (category, difficulty, question_text, correct_answer, wrong_answers, language, is_active, explanation) VALUES
('cinema', 5, 'Has any film ever won the Palme d''Or, the Golden Lion, and the Best Picture Oscar?', 'No film has achieved this', ARRAY['Parasite', 'Amour', 'The Pianist'], 'en', true, 'No film in cinema history has won all three of these prestigious awards simultaneously.'),
('cinema', 5, 'Which cinematographer worked with Terrence Malick on The Tree of Life?', 'Emmanuel Lubezki', ARRAY['Roger Deakins', 'Robert Richardson', 'Vittorio Storaro'], 'en', true, 'Emmanuel Lubezki is known for his long flowing shots and natural lighting.'),
('cinema', 5, 'Which director made The Mirror in 1975, an experimental autobiographical film?', 'Andrei Tarkovsky', ARRAY['Ingmar Bergman', 'Federico Fellini', 'Béla Tarr'], 'en', true, 'The Mirror is a non-linear autobiographical film mixing memories, dreams, and poetry.'),
('cinema', 5, 'Which Taiwanese filmmaker directed Yi Yi, considered a contemporary cinema masterpiece?', 'Edward Yang', ARRAY['Hou Hsiao-hsien', 'Tsai Ming-liang', 'Ang Lee'], 'en', true, 'Edward Yang directed Yi Yi in 2000, a portrait of a Taiwanese family across generations.'),
('cinema', 5, 'What term describes the semiotic cinema theory developed by Christian Metz?', 'The Grande Syntagmatique', ARRAY['Narrative diegesis', 'Structural analysis', 'Shot semiology'], 'en', true, 'Christian Metz developed this theory in his work Language and Cinema (1971).'),
('cinema', 5, 'Which Senegalese director is considered the father of African cinema?', 'Ousmane Sembène', ARRAY['Djibril Diop Mambéty', 'Souleymane Cissé', 'Med Hondo'], 'en', true, 'Ousmane Sembène directed the first sub-Saharan African feature film, Black Girl (1966).'),
('cinema', 5, 'What special lens was used to film Barry Lyndon by candlelight only?', 'Zeiss Planar 50mm f/0.7', ARRAY['Anamorphic lens', 'LED diffusion', 'Diffusion filter'], 'en', true, 'Kubrick used NASA Zeiss f/0.7 lenses to film scenes entirely by candlelight.'),
('cinema', 5, 'Which 1975 Chantal Akerman film is a classic of feminist cinema?', 'Jeanne Dielman, 23 quai du Commerce, 1080 Bruxelles', ARRAY['Les Rendez-vous d''Anna', 'Je, tu, il, elle', 'News from Home'], 'en', true, 'This 3-hour-21-minute film shows the routine daily life of a housewife in Brussels.'),
('cinema', 5, 'Which Soviet filmmaker developed the concept of Kino-Eye?', 'Dziga Vertov', ARRAY['Sergei Eisenstein', 'Lev Kuleshov', 'Alexander Medvedkin'], 'en', true, 'Vertov believed the camera could see truth better than the human eye.'),
('cinema', 5, 'Which Malian director made Yeelen, awarded at Cannes in 1987?', 'Souleymane Cissé', ARRAY['Ousmane Sembène', 'Idrissa Ouedraogo', 'Abderrahmane Sissako'], 'en', true, 'Yeelen won the Jury Prize at Cannes, a first for a sub-Saharan African film.'),
('cinema', 5, 'Which filmmaker made Soy Cuba, rediscovered by Scorsese and Coppola?', 'Mikhail Kalatozov', ARRAY['Sergei Parajanov', 'Andrei Tarkovsky', 'Elem Klimov'], 'en', true, 'Soy Cuba (1964) is a Soviet-Cuban film famous for its virtuoso long takes.'),
('cinema', 5, 'Which Argentine director made the 13-hour film La Flor?', 'Mariano Llinás', ARRAY['Lucrecia Martel', 'Lisandro Alonso', 'Pablo Trapero'], 'en', true, 'La Flor (2018) is an experimental film of over 13 hours divided into 6 episodes.'),
('cinema', 5, 'What is the LED wall technology used for virtual production called?', 'The Volume (StageCraft)', ARRAY['Green screen', 'Rear projection', 'Matte painting'], 'en', true, 'The Volume uses LED screens to create real-time realistic environments, popularized by The Mandalorian.'),
('cinema', 5, 'Which Portuguese director made the 6-hour film Vitalina Varela?', 'Pedro Costa', ARRAY['Manoel de Oliveira', 'Miguel Gomes', 'João Pedro Rodrigues'], 'en', true, 'Pedro Costa is known for his films about Cape Verdean communities in Lisbon.'),
('cinema', 5, 'Which film theorist wrote What is Cinema? in 4 volumes?', 'André Bazin', ARRAY['Christian Metz', 'Jean Mitry', 'Gilles Deleuze'], 'en', true, 'André Bazin co-founded Cahiers du Cinéma and was a major theorist of cinematic realism.'),
('cinema', 5, 'Which Sergei Parajanov film is a visual poem about an Armenian poet?', 'The Color of Pomegranates', ARRAY['Shadows of Forgotten Ancestors', 'The Legend of Suram Fortress', 'Ashik Kerib'], 'en', true, 'The Color of Pomegranates (1969) is a non-narrative film of exceptional visual beauty.'),
('cinema', 5, 'Which filmmaker coined the concept of caméra-stylo in a famous essay?', 'Alexandre Astruc', ARRAY['André Bazin', 'François Truffaut', 'Jean-Luc Godard'], 'en', true, 'Alexandre Astruc published the essay Birth of a New Avant-Garde: The Camera-Pen in 1948.'),
('cinema', 5, 'What is the original IMAX format used by Christopher Nolan for certain scenes?', '15-perf 70mm', ARRAY['35mm anamorphic', '65mm standard', 'Super 16mm'], 'en', true, 'The IMAX 15/70 format uses images 10 times larger than standard 35mm.'),
('cinema', 5, 'Which Cambodian filmmaker documented the Khmer Rouge aftermath in S21?', 'Rithy Panh', ARRAY['Apichatpong Weerasethakul', 'Lav Diaz', 'Tsai Ming-liang'], 'en', true, 'Rithy Panh directed S21: The Khmer Rouge Killing Machine, a chilling documentary on the genocide.'),
('cinema', 5, 'Which theoretical concept did Laura Mulvey develop in her 1975 essay?', 'The male gaze', ARRAY['Narrative suture', 'Primary identification', 'Feminist off-screen space'], 'en', true, 'Laura Mulvey theorized the male gaze in her essay Visual Pleasure and Narrative Cinema.');
